           <dd>The standard library and nothing else. The module must not import any file from the grader, so it runs on its own. Functions validate their inputs. The three statement functions never print, <code>post</code> never changes its argument, and <code>balance_sheet</code> returns a new dict on each call. <strong>Every named error condition raises <code>ValueError</code></strong>; the grader checks the exception type and not the wording of the message. The named conditions are these. <code>post</code> raises for a transaction without a date or without lines; a date that is not in the form YYYY-MM-DD or is not a real calendar date; an empty list of lines; a line without an account, a debit or a credit; an account outside the chart, including an account name that is not text; an amount that is not an integer, including a boolean (on either side) or a float such as <code>100.0</code>; a negative amount; a line with both a debit and a credit, of any sizes, or with neither; and an entry whose debits do not equal its credits. Each of the three statement functions and the articulation check raises for a period end that is not a month end, which means the last day of a calendar month in the form YYYY-MM-DD with no surrounding spaces. A year divisible by 4 is a leap year, except that a year divisible by 100 is a leap year only when it is also divisible by 400: so 2000-02-29 is a month end, 2100-02-28 is one, and 2100-02-29 is not a date. Money is never converted and never adjusted: the engine reports the cents it is given.</dd>
